WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:03.537
[Michael Curry] <i> Everybody thought home
computers were a really, really cool thing</i>

00:00:03.604 --> 00:00:06.206
<i>that only nerdy people
were ever gonna be into...</i>

00:00:06.273 --> 00:00:08.542
<i>3D printers are on that same kind of arc.</i>

00:00:10.377 --> 00:00:13.313 line:5%
We're out to fuel
the next industrial revolution...

00:00:15.015 --> 00:00:19.086 line:5%
<i>by putting the power to manufacture things
in your hands.</i>

00:00:22.089 --> 00:00:23.490 line:5%
[Barack Obama] <i> 3D printing
has the potential</i>

00:00:23.557 --> 00:00:26.426 line:5%
to revolutionize
the way we make almost everything.

00:00:26.493 --> 00:00:28.428 line:5%
Some of the developments
that come from the 3D printer

00:00:28.495 --> 00:00:31.565
<i>might put the first person
to create that device</i>

00:00:31.632 --> 00:00:34.334
<i>on the pedestal of
"major social innovator."</i>

00:00:34.401 --> 00:00:36.637 line:4%
Every day, I get inspired by people

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:39.373
<i>who have MakerBots
and are doing amazing things.</i>

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:43.143
[Chuck Pettis] <i> He grew up in
an entrepreneurial household.</i>

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:45.412
So he saw things getting produced.

00:00:45.479 --> 00:00:49.049
[Jeff Osborn] <i> People who run
successful, small technology companies...</i>

00:00:49.116 --> 00:00:51.485
<i>pretty much have to be crazy.</i>

00:00:51.551 --> 00:00:53.387
When we started, we were the only one.

00:00:53.453 --> 00:00:56.657
<i>Now we've got the big guys
and then we've got lots of small guys</i>

00:00:56.723 --> 00:00:58.558
<i>that think we're the big guys.</i>

00:00:58.625 --> 00:01:00.560 line:4%
Formlabs basically started...

00:01:00.627 --> 00:01:03.363
<i>in the basement of the house
that David and I were living in.</i>

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:06.667
I thought, "This is a quintessential geek
we are bringing up."

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:08.568
<i>Obsessed with what he is doing.</i>

00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:10.003
[Brad Feld] <i> If you're a leader,</i>

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:14.207
<i>every day there is something new
that comes up and smacks you in the face.</i>

00:01:16.076 --> 00:01:17.678
[Cody Wilson] <i> Welcome to the age
of the printed magazine.</i>

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:21.682
I'm gonna introduce you to
one of the most dangerous men on Earth.

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:23.350
[Cody Wilson] <i> We're
information anarchists.</i>

00:01:23.417 --> 00:01:25.452
<i>There should be one law.
If the police can have it,</i>

00:01:25.519 --> 00:01:28.155
if the military can have it,
then you can have it.

00:01:28.221 --> 00:01:29.523
[Anthony Moschella] <i> Somebody gets murdered
with a MakerBoted handgun...</i>

00:01:29.589 --> 00:01:30.590
Then what happens?

00:01:30.657 --> 00:01:34.695
[Osborn] <i> His iron rule, we don't talk
about 3D printed guns. Period.</i>

00:01:34.761 --> 00:01:37.564
We didn't have to say,
"This is our response to the gun thing."

00:01:37.631 --> 00:01:38.632
<i>It was just, "Hey, look at this."</i>

00:01:38.699 --> 00:01:41.134
[Brad Kenney] <i> Robohand was
worth talking about.</i>

00:01:41.201 --> 00:01:43.437
<i>Did it get half the pick-up
of the DEFCAD stuff?</i>

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:45.238
<i>Controversy sells.</i>

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.376
We were all inventing
what was gonna come next.

00:01:49.443 --> 00:01:52.746
[Feld] <i> A great partner
will turn into a horrible enemy.</i>

00:01:52.813 --> 00:01:54.347
<i>A company you've never heard of before</i>

00:01:54.414 --> 00:01:56.516
<i>will come out with something
that changes the game.</i>

00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:58.218
[Steve Jobs] <i> Every once in a while,</i>

00:01:58.285 --> 00:02:02.522
<i>a revolutionary product comes along
that changes everything.</i>

